  "id": "Compound::DB01246 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Alimemazine is implicated in the regulation of Cyp3a4 through a series of interconnected pathways involving autonomic dysfunction and electrocardiogram abnormalities. The evidence suggests that Alimemazine may act as a causal agent in the development of these conditions, which in turn lead to binding with Cyp3a4. The lowest common ancestors of Alimemazine and its downstream targets, such as Prochlorperazine and Dolasetron, are both classified under the category of \"Agent Affecting Nervous System\" and \"Organic Heteropolycyclic Compound,\" indicating a shared biological role in nervous system function. This suggests that Alimemazine may influence Cyp3a4 through a mechanism that involves the nervous system, potentially by modulating the expression or activity of Cyp3a4 in response to these conditions. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Alimemazine in the regulation of Cyp3a4, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
